  "question": {
    "text": "If the ratio of lengths, radii and Young's moduli of steel and brass wires in the figure are $a, b$ and $c$ respectively, then the corresponding ratio of increase in their lengths is :\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0095_b6c69a0a6a13.png\"><br>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3 c}{2 a b^2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2 a^2 c}{b}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3 a}{2 b^2 c}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2 a c}{b^2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to questions,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\ell_{\\mathrm{s}}}{\\ell_{\\mathrm{b}}}=\\mathrm{a}, \\frac{\\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{s}}}{\\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{b}}}=\\mathrm{b}, \\frac{\\mathrm{y}_{\\mathrm{s}}}{\\mathrm{y}_{\\mathrm{b}}}=\\mathrm{c}, \\frac{\\Delta \\ell \\mathrm{s}}{\\Delta \\ell_{\\mathrm{b}}}=? \\\\\n& \\text { As, } \\mathrm{y}=\\frac{\\mathrm{F} \\ell}{\\mathrm{A} \\Delta \\ell} \\Rightarrow \\Delta \\ell=\\frac{\\mathrm{F} \\ell}{\\mathrm{Ay}} \\\\\n& \\Delta \\ell_{\\mathrm{s}}=\\frac{3 \\mathrm{mg} \\ell_{\\mathrm{s}}}{\\pi \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{s}}^2 \\cdot \\mathrm{y}_{\\mathrm{s}}}\\left[\\because \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{s}}=(\\mathrm{M}+2 \\mathrm{M}) \\mathrm{g}\\right] \\\\\n& \\Delta \\ell_{\\mathrm{b}}=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{Mg}\\ell_{\\mathrm{b}}}{\\pi \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{b}}^2 \\cdot \\mathrm{y}_{\\mathrm{b}}}\\left[\\because \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{b}}=2 \\mathrm{Mg}\\right]\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\therefore \\frac{\\Delta \\ell_{\\mathrm{s}}}{\\Delta \\ell_{\\mathrm{b}}}=\\frac{\\frac{3 \\mathrm{Mg} \\ell_{\\mathrm{s}}}{\\pi \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{s}}^2 \\cdot \\mathrm{y}_{\\mathrm{s}}}}{\\frac{2 \\mathrm{Mg} \\cdot \\ell_{\\mathrm{b}}}{\\pi \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{b}}^2 \\cdot \\mathrm{y}_{\\mathrm{b}}}}=\\frac{3 \\mathrm{a}}{2 \\mathrm{b}^2 \\mathrm{C}}$"
  }
}